## AIOS QEMU interleaved soak (text mode)

**Status:** finished (2 boots)

### Settings

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Design | 2 arms (A, B), 1 rounds of one boot per arm: 2 boots |
| Rotation | the arm order moves by one each round: A B |
| Boots | 35s each, stall limit 15s, data disk fresh per boot |
| QEMU | QEMU emulator version 99.1.0 (aios test fake) (`<ROOT>/bin/qemu-system-aarch64`, sha256 `83bc1911cc1b14e1`) |
| Firmware | `<ROOT>/fw.fd` (sha256 `c3bf47ea1f4a4a60`) |
| Host | <HOST> |
| Load average | <L> |
| Load check | passed: load1 0.50 before the builds, not above the host's CPU count (AIOS_SOAK_LOADAVG override: every load reads '0.50 0.40 0.30') |
| Toolchains | mixed allowed (--allow-mixed-toolchains): the arms' channels and compilers may differ |
| Build | skipped (--no-build): each arm boots the ESP image already in its checkout, not one built from the checked commit |
| Parent cargo config | <CARGO-CONFIG> |
| Arm base | every arm contains `244166f03dbd262e5ed2921769fb515ee7dd0652` (AIOS_SOAK_MIN_ARM_BASE override; the release base is `7167d408f6a43ca9859fb6238f608ca6bdee37d6`, #196); checked on each checkout's HEAD, not on the ESP image that boots (--no-build) |
| Harness | <HARNESS> |
| Logs | `<ROOT>/repo/out` |

### Arms

| Arm | Checkout | Commit | Channel | rustc | Kernel |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| A | `../arms/a` | `244166f` | nightly-2026-10-09 | rustc 1.99.0-nightly (fake 2026-10-09) | kernel ELF sha256 `94cc3f95c7b1a13c` |
| B | `../arms/b` | `244166f-dirty` | nightly-2026-10-01 | rustc 1.98.0-nightly (fake 2026-10-01) | kernel ELF sha256 `94cc3f95c7b1a13c` |

### Classes per arm

| Class | A | B |
|---|---:|---:|
| PCZERO | 0 | 0 |
| PANIC-LOCK | 0 | 0 |
| PANIC | 1 | 0 |
| EXCEPTION | 0 | 1 |
| WEDGE-STUCK | 0 | 0 |
| WEDGE-ALIVE | 0 | 0 |
| INCONCLUSIVE | 0 | 0 |
| DEGRADED | 0 | 0 |
| CLEAN | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | 1 | 1 |
| CLEAN rate | 0% (95% Wilson interval 0%-79%) | 0% (95% Wilson interval 0%-79%) |

The CLEAN rate is over each arm's conclusive boots (INCONCLUSIVE left out).

### Load

The host's 1-minute load average before each boot.

| Arm | Boots with a load | load1 mean | load1 max |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| A | 1 | 0.50 | 0.50 |
| B | 1 | 0.50 | 0.50 |

A pair whose arms' mean loads differ by more than 25% of the lower mean is redone: the load, not the change, may explain its differences.

- A vs B: 0.50 vs 0.50, 0% apart: comparable

### Pair tests

Fisher's exact test on conclusive boots only (INCONCLUSIVE is left out of every count and denominator). In each pair the earlier arm is the previous one and the later arm the new one. The regression guard fails when the new arm has fewer CLEAN boots with one-sided p < 0.05. A class is marked `removed` when the new arm has none of it and the one-sided p (fewer in new) < 0.05, and `new` when the previous arm has none of it and the one-sided p (more in new) < 0.05. The rate differences (new - previous, in percentage points) are recorded, never gated on.

#### A vs B (A previous, B new)

**Regression guard:** CLEAN 0/1 in A, 0/1 in B; one-sided p (fewer CLEAN in B) = 1: passes

| Class | A | B | B - A | p fewer in B | p more in B | p two-sided | Marker |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| PCZERO | 0/1 | 0/1 | 0 pp | 1 | 1 | 1 | - |
| PANIC-LOCK | 0/1 | 0/1 | 0 pp | 1 | 1 | 1 | - |
| PANIC | 1/1 | 0/1 | -100 pp | 0.5 | 1 | 1 | - |
| EXCEPTION | 0/1 | 1/1 | +100 pp | 1 | 0.5 | 1 | - |
| WEDGE-STUCK | 0/1 | 0/1 | 0 pp | 1 | 1 | 1 | - |
| WEDGE-ALIVE | 0/1 | 0/1 | 0 pp | 1 | 1 | 1 | - |
| DEGRADED | 0/1 | 0/1 | 0 pp | 1 | 1 | 1 | - |
| CLEAN | 0/1 | 0/1 | 0 pp | 1 | 1 | 1 | - |

